{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1532897155,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNDU1NjEzODM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2716","origin":"github"},"title":"ZeroDivisionError when publishing an empty file for the first time","message":"#### What is the problem?\nIn some situations, I want to publish empty files to a Google Drive remote, sibling to a GitHub remote. However, when publishing the file, although the file is correctly transferred to the given remotes, a ZeroDivisionError is raised.\n`[ERROR  ] float division by zero [annexrepo.py:get_size_from_perc_complete:3625] (ZeroDivisionError) `\n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n1. In a dataset, create an empty file with `touch zero.txt`\n2. `datalad save zero.txt`\n3. `datalad publish --to github --transfer-data all`\n#### What version of DataLad are you using?\nVersion: datalad 0.10.1\nOperating system: Ubuntu 18.04 LTS\n#### Is there anything else that would be useful to know in this context?\nThis error appears to happen only when publishing a 0 byte file **for the first time**. Using `datalad remove` to remove the file and publishing a new empty file afterwards do not cause the error.","files":null}]}